PASS D3c control: the 24 pair permutations (x) id on token 3 give minimum 0 >= 0 (exclusion needs coupling into the extra token)
PASS D4a mutation: ancilla tests restricted to the x-axis states give minimum 0 >= 0 over that family (the axis witness of B3a uses a non-real ancilla test)
PASS D4b real non-axis tests suffice for the real fixture z_(1,1): a=(2,1), b=(1,2), c=(3,1) give -47/4 < 0 (normalized -47/1000)
PASS D4c configuration-only tests (all three tokens in {|0>,|1>}) give minimum 0 >= 0 on every defect and on Gamma(Phi+): the exclusion needs non-configuration token tests
